---
import Callout from '../../../../../components/Callout.astro';
import Code from '../../../../../components/Code.astro';
import ReplyTask from '../../../../../components/ReplyTask.astro';
import SessionPage from '../../../../../components/SessionPage.astro';
import SessionSection from '../../../../../components/SessionSection.astro';
import { session } from './_session.ts';

const model = `public interface INotifier
{
    void Send(string message);
}

public sealed class ConsoleNotifier : INotifier
{
    public void Send(string message) => Console.WriteLine(message);
}`;

const shapeOnly = `public sealed class ShapeOnlyNotifier
{
    public void Send(string message) => Console.WriteLine(message);
}

INotifier notifier = new ShapeOnlyNotifier();
// CS0029: Cannot implicitly convert type 'ShapeOnlyNotifier' to 'INotifier'`;

const broken = `public interface IPriceLabel
{
    string Format(decimal amount);
}

public sealed class UsdPriceLabel : IPriceLabel
{
    // Add the missing member here.
}

// CS0535: 'UsdPriceLabel' does not implement interface member
// 'IPriceLabel.Format(decimal)'`;
---

<SessionPage session={session}
  title="Session 9 · C#: nominal interface contracts"
  heading="Make an interface contract explicit"
  lede="In C#, matching method names are not enough. A class names the interface it implements, then provides every required member."
  backHref="/topics/csharp/"
  backLabel="C# sessions"
>
  <SessionSection title="Read a complete implementation">
    <Code code={model} lang="csharp" />
    <p><code>INotifier</code> is the contract. The colon says that <code>ConsoleNotifier</code> promises to implement it. The public <code>Send</code> method keeps that promise.</p>
  </SessionSection>

  <SessionSection title="The key difference from TypeScript">
    <Code code={shapeOnly} lang="csharp" />
    <Callout>
      TypeScript often accepts a value because its shape matches. C# interfaces are nominal here: the class must explicitly name the interface. It must also provide all required members.
    </Callout>
  </SessionSection>

  <SessionSection title="A missing-member failure">
    <Code code={broken} lang="csharp" />
    <p>The class names <code>IPriceLabel</code>, so the compiler checks the promise. The error tells you the exact member that is missing.</p>
  </SessionSection>

  <ReplyTask id="learn:csharp/009:q1" difficulty={3}>
    <ol>
      <li>Add one public <code>Format</code> method inside <code>UsdPriceLabel</code>. It must return an amount such as <code>$12.50</code>.</li>
      <li>In one short sentence, say why another class with the same <code>Format</code> method does not automatically implement <code>IPriceLabel</code>.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Reply with the method and one sentence. Do not rewrite the interface.</p>
  </ReplyTask>
</SessionPage>
